        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Miscellaneous taxes, soybeans: 1.832 koku. The double-column interlinear note reads 'valued at 4 to 8 gō per ryō', that is 0.408 koku of soybeans to the ryō; 1.832 ÷ 0.408 = 4.4902 ryō, which is exactly the 4.4902 kan-mon recorded to the right. The full-width closing parenthesis printed below the note closes the large bracket opened at the 一本 note, making this the ninth and last of the bracketed lines."
